menu "Lua scripting"

config LUA_ENABLE
    bool "Lua runtime"
    default n
    help
      NOT IMPLEMENTED YET (phase 6). Device protocols are meant to live in Lua
      on LittleFS so they can be changed without a program/erase cycle; only
      the stable pieces (crypto, checksums, TLV primitives) stay in C.

config LUA_HEAP_KB
    int "Lua arena (KB)"
    depends on LUA_ENABLE
    default 160
    help
      A dedicated static arena, not the system heap, so a runaway script hits
      its own ceiling with an ordinary Lua out-of-memory error instead of
      starving lwIP or BTstack. Static so the link-time RAM check can see it.

      Raised from 96 after measurement, not guesswork. COMPILING a module
      costs far more than running it: the 28 KB A2687 profile peaks at 82 KB
      of arena while the parser works, against about 14 KB once it is
      resident. At 96 KB that loaded only into a completely empty arena and
      failed with "not enough memory" the moment any other script was also
      loaded -- which is the normal state of a board being worked on.

      The cost is bss, which this part has to spare.

      Raised again to 160 for the advertisement-driven Anker stack, and this
      time the earlier advice -- split it into modules rather than raise the
      ceiling -- had already been taken and was not enough. That stack loads
      one module per stage and unloads each before the next compiles, so the
      COMPILE peak is well under control. What is left is steady residency:
      the driver, the link, the schema decoder and one per-model table come
      to about 74 KB live while streaming.

      The failure at 128 KB was not exhaustion but FRAGMENTATION -- roughly
      56 KB free and still no block large enough, after a report that builds
      ~68 TLV item tables every few seconds. Live heap was flat across polls,
      which is how you tell the two apart. A first-fit arena cannot do much
      about that except have room to breathe.

config LUA_HOOK_BUDGET
    int "Instructions per scheduler slice before a script is forced to yield"
    depends on LUA_ENABLE
    default 20000

endmenu
